TITLE:: RolandOTA
summary:: Virtual Analog Model of the Roland IR3109 4-Stage OTA Cascade VCF
categories:: UGens>Filters
related:: Guides/Filtra, Classes/CS80, Classes/Wasp, Classes/MS20OTA

DESCRIPTION::
RolandOTA is a virtual analog model of the 4-pole (24 dB/octave) low-pass filter based on the custom Roland IR3109 integrated circuit, famously featured in the Juno-6, Juno-60, Jupiter-8, and SH-101 synthesizers.

The circuit topology consists of four cascaded 1st-order operational transconductance amplifier (OTA) integrators enclosed in a global negative feedback loop. At high resonance settings (res >= 1.0), the filter enters autonomous sinusoidal self-oscillation. Each OTA stage incorporates hyperbolic tangent (tanh) soft-saturation corresponding to the bipolar differential transistor pair.

RolandOTA features an authentic simulation of the natural "bass drop" characteristic of vintage Roland ladders under high resonance, along with an optional strong>resComp:: parameter to compensate for low-frequency attenuation when modern punch is required.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: in
Audio-rate input signal.

ARGUMENT:: freq
Filter cutoff frequency in Hertz (10 Hz to 0.49 * sampleRate). Supports audio rate and control rate. Default: 1000.0.

ARGUMENT:: res
Resonance parameter in [0.0, 1.2]. Self-oscillation occurs at res >= 1.0. Default: 0.0.

ARGUMENT:: drive
Overdrive factor (default 1.0, range [0.01, 20.0]). Controls input and inter-stage OTA saturation depth.

ARGUMENT:: resComp
Resonance bass-loss compensation factor in [0.0, 1.0].
When set to 0.0, displays authentic vintage Roland bass attenuation as resonance increases.
When set to 1.0, actively compensates low frequencies, maintaining low-end energy while ringing. Default: 0.0.

returns:: An audio-rate filtered signal.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
s.boot;

// 1. Classic Juno/Jupiter 4-pole Low-Pass Acid Sweep
(
x = {
    var saw = Saw.ar([110, 110.5]) * 0.25;
    var cutoff = SinOsc.kr(0.2).exprange(150, 4500);
    RolandOTA.ar(saw, freq: cutoff, res: 0.85, drive: 1.5, resComp: 0.0) * 0.4;
}.play;
)

// 2. Bass-Loss Compensation (resComp = 0 vs 1)
(
x = {
    var bass = Pulse.ar(55, 0.4) * 0.3 ! 2;
    var toggle = LFPulse.kr(0.5); // alternates every 2 seconds
    RolandOTA.ar(bass, freq: 800, res: 0.9, drive: 1.0, resComp: toggle) * 0.4;
}.play;
)

// 3. Singing Self-Oscillation Sine Melody
(
x = {
    var trig = Impulse.ar(0);
    var pitch = Demand.kr(Impulse.kr(4), 0, Dseq([440, 554.37, 659.25, 880], inf));
    RolandOTA.ar(trig * 0.1, freq: pitch, res: 1.05, drive: 1.0) * 0.5 ! 2;
}.play;
)
::
